From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Jul 2026 02:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clocksource: sky1: defer probe on missing timer clocks

Confirmed live on Orion O6N 2026-07-19/20: sky1_timer_probe()
already uses dev_err_probe() correctly here (unlike the 7.2 kernel's
older implementation, which hard-returns -EINVAL and discards the
real error) but is still missing the -ENOENT-to-EPROBE_DEFER
translation, so a clock not yet mapped by clk-sky1-acpi at probe
time is still treated as a terminal failure rather than retried.

Same fix class as 2021-2024 (linlondp/usb3-phy/cdnsp-sky1/cdns-i2c).

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c
index df9db89..83f6fa0 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sky1-gpt.c
@@ -221,7 +221,9 @@ static int sky1_timer_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		sky1tm->pclk = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(dev,
 							"fch_timer_apb_clk");
 	if (IS_ERR(sky1tm->pclk))
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(sky1tm->pclk),
+		return dev_err_probe(dev,
+				     PTR_ERR(sky1tm->pclk) == -ENOENT ?
+				     -EPROBE_DEFER : PTR_ERR(sky1tm->pclk),
 				     "failed to get apb clock\n");
 
 	sky1tm->tclk = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev, "func");
@@ -229,7 +231,9 @@ static int sky1_timer_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		sky1tm->tclk = devm_clk_get_enabled(dev,
 						     "fch_timer_func_clk");
 	if (IS_ERR(sky1tm->tclk))
-		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(sky1tm->tclk),
+		return dev_err_probe(dev,
+				     PTR_ERR(sky1tm->tclk) == -ENOENT ?
+				     -EPROBE_DEFER : PTR_ERR(sky1tm->tclk),
 				     "failed to get func clock\n");
 
 	rate = clk_get_rate(sky1tm->tclk);
--
